items.text:
Construct meaning from a variety of grade appropriate contemporary and classical texts, including:
• fiction and non-fiction (including a novel and another full-length text*);
• written, oral, visual and multimodal;
• descriptive, narrative, poetic, expository and persuasive;
• texts from diverse and historically underrepresented voices, reflecting a range of geographical locations, cultures, worldviews and lived experiences; and,
• texts that address identity, social responsibility and social agency (action).

Develop a variety of original compositions, including:
• fiction and non-fiction;
• written, oral, visual and multimodal;
• descriptive, narrative, expository, poetic and persuasive; and,
• compositions that address identity, social responsibility and social agency (action).
